{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>This they shall give.</b> He showed him something like a coin of fire and its weight was a half-shekel, and He said to him: 'Like this they shall give' (Jerusalem Talmud, Shekalim 1:1)." "<b>When you count those who are numbered.</b> The way of those who count is to pass those counted one after another, and so ״all that passes under the rod״ (Leviticus 27), and so ״the flock shall pass under the hand of the one counting״ (Jeremiah 33)." "<b>A half-shekel, by the shekel of the sanctuary.</b> By the weight of the shekel that I have fixed for you to weigh sacred shekels with — such as the shekels spoken of in the section of valuations and the field of inheritance." "<b>Twenty gerais the shekel.</b> Now He has explained to you how much it is." "<b>A gerah.</b> A term for a ma'ah; and so in Samuel (I Samuel 2): ״they would come to bow to him for an agorat of silver and a loaf of bread.״" "<b>Twenty gerah the shekel.</b> The full shekel is four zuzim, and the zuz from the start was five ma'ot — but they came and added a sixth to it and raised it to six ma'ot silver. And half of this shekel that I have told you — they shall give it as a terumah to HaShem (Bekhorot 50a)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:48.881606053Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}